---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../../../config';
---
<Base title="Privacy Policy | CQ Buddy" description="What we collect (very little), why, and what we never do: no ad trackers, no data selling, no dark patterns.">
  <section>
    <div class="container" style="max-width:760px;">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="muted small">Last updated: 4 November 2026 · v1.0</p>
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>What we collect</h2>
        <p>Only what you give us to do the job: your name, travel dates, party size, flight number if you share it, and your WhatsApp or email address. That's the whole list.</p>
        <h2>What we never do</h2>
        <p>We don't run advertising trackers. We don't sell, rent or trade your data. We don't add you to any newsletter you didn't ask for.</p>
        <h2>Where it lives</h2>
        <p>Booking details live in our own WhatsApp Business and email systems, accessed only by team members handling your service. This website itself stores nothing about you — the booking form has no server; it opens WhatsApp on your own device.</p>
        <h2>Retention</h2>
        <p>We keep booking records as long as local law reasonably requires (tax and accounting), then delete. You can ask what we hold about you, or ask us to delete it, any time at <a href={`mailto:${site.supportEmail}`}>{site.supportEmail}</a>.</p>
        <h2>Third parties</h2>
        <p>WhatsApp (Meta) processes messages under its own policy. Payment handling, when online payment launches, will sit with a licensed payment provider — this page gets updated before that goes live.</p>
        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>If we ever change this policy in a way that matters, we say so in the booking confirmation — silence is not consent.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
